WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.334
-It's so nice to see you
in person.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.434
-Yeah, yeah. It's really great
to be here.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:05.534
-Thank you for being here.
-No problem.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.300
-I want to get into everything.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.901
I want to talk about the new
series, but I also follow you

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:13.801
on the socials, and I like to
follow you on there.

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:16.133
And you had a good -- Kind of
now and then you just

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.767
throw a throwback Thursday
photo, and I go,

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.701
"Oh, we should talk about that
next time."

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.701
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Next time you're on the show.

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:29.334
And you posted one on Instagram
of a "Mean Girls" karaoke party.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.701
-I know. I thought that would --

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:33.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:35.200
I thought it was a good one.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.968
-Lacey Chabert, Amy Poehler,
Lindsay Lohan.

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:39.501
I mean, that's a classic
right there.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.434
-Also, it'd never been seen.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.634
I thought I found gold
in my closet.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:46.133
I was back in L.A., shooting
"The Dropout" and I was

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.567
going through all these pictures
trying to throw [bleep] away,

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.400
and I was just like,
"This is gold. We need to --"

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.200
-"Someone needs to see this."
-Yeah, this was my first

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.801
wrap party, and there was
karaoke with these fine folks.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:58.701
-Do you do karaoke a lot?
-I don't.

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:00.167
-You do not, no.
-I don't like it.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.801
-But you're a good singer.
I've heard you sing in movies.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.501
-Thanks, I know.
I would do it for work.

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:07.667
I wouldn't want to ever force
people to listen to me.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.834
Not on my watch,
you know what I mean?

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.968
[ Laughter ]
-But that's the fun of karaoke.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.501
We're all kind of paying
for entertainment from you,

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.334
from everybody.
-But some people take it

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:19.133
really seriously,
and then I feel like an idiot.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.934
I'm too worried about what
people think of me.

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:25.267
So I will do, like, Eminem,
or I'll do something that's fun.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:26.434
-You'll do something
that's kind of like,

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:27.834
"Don't take this serious."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:30.868
I'm definitely not good at this,
so therefore I'm going to do it.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.767
-Oh, I'm the opposite.
-Are you competitive?

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:36.067
-I'm really trying to get
my album out.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.534
[ Laughter ]
-Interesting.

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:40.133
-"Yo, if there's any producers
out there, check this out."

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.801
♪ Don't stop ♪
I'm going for it.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:46.167
-But you can carry a tune, so
it's not -- It wouldn't be hard.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.501
-Do you sing around the house?

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.100
-Yeah, I only sing things that
are stuck in my head,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.167
which are like --
♪ Mira, Mira, Mira, Mira ♪

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:55.501
♪ Royal detective ♪

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:59.434
Or ♪ Hey, Gabby ♪

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:00.501
Does anybody know?
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:01.701
-♪ Welcome to the dollhouse ♪

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.434
-"Gabby's Dollhouse"
is the greatest. Come on.

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.501
-No, it's a great show,
and I love watching it.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:06.868
I really do.

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:09.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.334
-That is such funny reaction.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.467
"No, I just love it so much!"

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:17.501
-I will tell you, I listened to
"Encanto" album

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:20.100
when I was in Barcelona --
away from my kids last week.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.601
-Just 'cause you love it.
-Because I love it so much.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.501
I do. I love it.

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:27.234
-You've been acting, believe it
or not, over 20 years.

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.767
Does that seem possible?

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:30.234
No.
-I don't --

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:31.667
-I don't believe that, yeah.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.501
But I heard there was one job

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.300
early on that you missed out
on getting.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.501
And I just want to hear
a little about this.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.868
-Oh, good, the -- Yeah, I
auditioned for, like,

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:42.200
Clean &amp; Clear and Neutrogena
and whatever else was there.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.234
-You were just modeling first.
-Target commercial.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:45.968
I really wanted to be part of
the Target commercials

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:47.801
because they were, like,
national commercials,

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.601
and you got paid a lot of money.

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:52.000
-Yeah, Target,
they make great commercials.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.934
-Yeah, they do, and then make
you do weird stuff

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:56.601
in the auditions too.
-Like what?

00:02:56.601 --> 00:03:00.601
-Like, "What's your
secret talent?" for instance.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:03.167
And I was probably 15
or younger,

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:05.701
and they put on some
Timberlake song.

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:08.200
And I was like,
"I'm not going to dance,

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.501
but I can do the robot."

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.367
[ Laughter ]
That's another thing.

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:14.167
This is very related to my fear
of, like, singing.

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:16.734
I'll just rap for you.
You want me to dance?

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:19.167
I'm not going to dance for you,
but I'll do the robot.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.534
You know what I mean?
-Okay, yeah, so you don't dance,

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.701
you don't sing, but you do,
though, sing, in real life.

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:25.400
I've heard you in movies.
-Yeah, for -- Yeah.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.834
-Yeah. And then robot comes out
when what, under pressure?

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:30.634
[ Laughter ]
-Uh-huh.

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.033
-Like weddings or something?

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:34.334
You're like, "Don't make me --
I don't really want to --"

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:37.234
So what if a beat just came on
right now, what would happen?

00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:38.534
-Uh...

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:40.534
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:44.234
I guess I would get up
and I would try to do the robot.

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:49.234
♪♪

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:51.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.400
♪♪

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.467
-You committed to
that first one.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.400
That's how you do it.
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.734
You really commit to it.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:03.634
-Thanks. It's hard.
-You're very good.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.434
-I love that you did that.

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:07.000
You really commit to it.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.367
By the way, you're getting
amazing reviews

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.334
for your role in "The Dropout."

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:14.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. It's a dream.

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:16.901
-Amanda Seyfried in
"a career-best performance,"

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:19.133
"Chicago Sun Times,"
not too shabby.

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:20.868
Career-best, wow.

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.934
I mean, you're fantastic.
-I guess I'm done.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:25.701
-"Spell-binding performance,"
"Sydney Morning Herald."

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:29.033
I mean, "terrifyingly
mesmerizes,"

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:30.501
"Hollywood Insider."

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:31.968
I mean, this is a big deal.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:33.567
-It's so crazy.

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.834
-Did you think the voice was
going to be the thing?

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:37.767
Did you think,
"Oh, I could just do her"?

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:39.734
Did you see the documentary?
How did you get into it?

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:41.167
-I did it all.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:45.234
I also had deposition tapes of
just a static camera on her

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:46.634
while she's being questioned
from the SCC.

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:49.434
-Fascinating character.
-Yeah, and you see a lot.

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:53.534
I mean, you see everything
in those tapes.

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:56.601
And I also did a lot of watching
every YouTube video

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:59.067
that was ever recorded of her
on stage.

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:00.667
And, you know, of course,

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.734
I watched everything
and listened to everything --

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:06.067
the Carreyrou book on Audible
and "The Dropout" podcast,

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.000
of course, which this is
based on.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.534
Man, I couldn't get enough.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.567
It was the most fun ever.
And you know what?

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.801
A bunch of my actor friends
were like,

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:16.033
"God, you're a character actor."

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:18.234
And I was like, "I never thought
of it that way."

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:21.300
It's so much more fun to play
people that are

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.901
a little bit separate
from who you are.

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:24.367
I'm always playing a version of
myself, right?

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:28.567
And I love it.
And I'm good at it, depending.

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:31.467
And this was just a completely
different ballgame,

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:34.300
and I really loved it.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.834
-And is it true that -- 'Cause I
remember the documentary,

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:38.467
watching that, and then going
like -- A lot of her friends

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:41.000
were like, "Yeah, that kind of
really was never her voice."

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.334
And then her eyes
just started --

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:45.167
She just started not blinking.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.200
She read that in some book
like if you blink,

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.968
it's sign of weakness
or something.

00:05:48.968 --> 00:05:51.868
-Yeah, something like that.
Like, you're not listening

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:54.667
or like just really,
I'm invested in you.

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:56.000
I want to know
what you're saying.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.901
-So she would just not blink,

00:05:57.901 --> 00:06:00.267
and she would come and just
stare and not blink.

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:03.501
And I was like, "Oh, my gosh,
it's fascinating."

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:05.767
And you kind of nailed it.
You really did a great job.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:06.934
-[ as Elizabeth Holmes ]
You got to get there, you know?

00:06:06.934 --> 00:06:08.234
It's really important.

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:09.367
[ Normal voice ] No, sorry.

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:11.300
It's not that deep.
Listen, it's my version.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.868
I always have to remind people
it's my version of it.

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:15.567
I will never be able to go
that low,

00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:18.200
but I will go as low as I can
with the affect.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.534
-You did. Perfect.

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:21.234
Yeah. Don't change.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:21.234 --> 00:06:24.334
Here's Amanda Seyfried in the
series finale of "The Dropout."

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:25.634
Take a look at this.

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:29.167
-You're just smearing it in.
Give it to me.

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:32.000
I think I'm very angry at you.
I am.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.801
I'm very angry.

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:39.834
-You told me that when you
visited me at school,

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:42.067
after everything that happened,

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:49.100
you told me to just put it away
and forget it.

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:56.367
If you choose to forget
certain things,

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:58.634
do you think that's lying?

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:01.934
-Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:01.934 --> 00:07:04.767
Amanda Seyfried, everybody!
-Such good writing.

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:06.734
-The series finale of
"The Dropout"

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:08.634
airs this Thursday on Hulu.

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:10.934
Amanda and I are doing
the whisper challenge

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:12.300
when we come back.
Stick around, everybody.

